    "result_text": "All tests pass. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the age-band feature for `POST /api/owners` / `GET /api/owners/{id}`, following the existing Spring/MapStruct/OpenAPI conventions in the codebase.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added `birthDate` (optional, `format: date`) as an input field on `OwnerFields`, and `ageBand` (readonly string) as a derived field on `Owner`. The DTOs are generated from this spec at build time.\n\n2. **`model/AgeBand.java`** (new) \u2014 A small enum encapsulating the single responsibility of age-band classification: `of(birthDate, asOf)` computes completed years via `Period` and maps to `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), or `SENIOR` (65+).\n\n3. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the persisted `birthDate` field (getter/setter) and a `@Transient getAgeBand()` that returns the band computed against `registrationDate`, or `null` when no birth date was supplied. The domain owns both dates, so the derivation lives there.\n\n4. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `ageBand` to `toOwnerDto` via a `resolveAgeBand` helper (null-safe enum\u2192string), matching the existing pattern for derived read-only fields like `contactPreference`. `birthDate` maps automatically (same type on both sides).\n\n5. **`db/{h2,hsqldb,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql`** \u2014 Added the `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table in all four dialects.\n\nThe whole test suite (the acceptance test, including the new `coreDerivesAgeBand` checkpoint) is green.",
